# Pull requests

## Title

Conventional Commits: `type(optional-scope): subject`, in English (`.cursor/rules/conventional-commits.mdc`).

## Body

Follow `.github/pull_request_template.md` with the same headings in the same order:

1. `## Summary`
2. `## Related`
3. `## Verification`
4. `## Measurements`
5. `## Risk / Rollback`
6. `## Checklist`

- The headings stay English. The body text may be Japanese (`.cursor/rules/language.mdc`).
- Empty sections say `N/A`; do not delete them.
- `## Related` has `Closes #N` alone on a line when the PR finishes the Issue, `Part of #N` when it does not (`.cursor/rules/github-closing.mdc`).
- `## Verification` names the commands that ran and their result: `./build.ps1`, the NativeAOT publish when the Issue names it, any search a "every X does Y" claim rests on (`.cursor/rules/spec-checks.mdc`). A search is written with the terms that were searched, and only a search that ran is written: a PR that says it searched for one name when it searched for a neighbouring one leaves the first name behind in the design.
- A search the body names runs before the body is written, over the whole repository, the rules and skills included. PR #223's body said that the design and the rules were searched for `BinOutput`; the search over `.cursor/rules/` ran after the PR was opened and found the name in `csharp.mdc`.
- A section the body says the PR changed, or a sample it says was compiled, is one that `git diff main...HEAD` shows. PR #77's body listed design §4.9 as changed and its example as compiled; the diff had no change to §4.9.
- A count the body gives ("the other 9 places") is the output of a command that selects exactly what the count names, not a reading of a broader search.
- `## Measurements` carries the numbers for a frame-path or data-path change: time per stage before and after, allocations per frame, bytes uploaded per frame, at the named data and viewport sizes, against a named baseline (`.cursor/rules/bench.mdc`). `N/A` only when nothing on those paths changed.
- A design PR's body lists the details decided while writing, not in the Grill (names, defaults, how a degenerate case is drawn), so that the owner can see and change them. PR #121's review asked for the list.
- Pass the body to `gh pr create` through a temporary UTF-8 file (`--body-file`), deleted after the call (`.cursor/rules/scratch.mdc`).

```text
# BAD — "Verification: searched for every caller" (no command, no terms)
# GOOD — "Verification: `rg -n 'ChunkIndex\.' src tests` — 7 callers, all updated"
```
